WEBVTT

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.050
How is Corporal Stark?

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:24.720
If you mean Rosie, she's still sleeping.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.030
I see.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.480
Perhaps that's for the best.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.430
It's strange.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.140
What is?

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.390
Losing friends, losing subordinates...

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:39.400
I still can't get used to these sorrowful feelings.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.380
Yeah, you can't get used to it.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:48.780
But don't let it show. You're the commander of an entire company now.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.910
Thanks, Largo.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:53.030
We've known each other for a long time.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:07.200
1935 AD, August 25th.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.540
Chapter 18

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.540
August Rain

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.730
The day of Isara Gunther's funeral.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:16.280
She was promoted two ranks, becoming a sergeant major. {souchou could refer to master sergeant too. not sure about ranks}

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:38.890
Welkin!

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.950
Everyone, thanks for today. {I would like to thank everyone today}

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.880
Allow me to thank you for being friends with Isara up until now.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:17.660
Isara's death is indeed quite saddening,

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.420
but I want everyone to forget about it quickly,

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.220
and continue to do their best as part of the militia.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:27.350
That's what Isara would have wished for.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.090
Thank you. Truly.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:29.600
Wait a minute!

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.810
She died because you didn't bring her with you!

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.280
Have you forgotten that?!

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:35.230
Don't screw with me!

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:38.240
You practically killed her yourself!

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.190
That's...

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:41.940
You didn't understand Isara's feelings at all!

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.200
She stayed up all night to make those smoke bombs!

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.080
Cut it out, Ramal.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.260
Yet you so easily... {he means like "Isara's death was nothing"}

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.310
I refuse!

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:52.170
Are you satisfied with your victory even though Isara died?!

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:56.460
Ramal, do you want to see her off with feelings of anger?

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:05.890
Sorry.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:08.350
It's okay. I didn't mind.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:30.530
Brother, what are you trying to look for?

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:33.420
Of course I'm looking for the rarer ones.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.840
By rarer ones, you mean...

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.570
Just shut up and look for it.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:44.000
Yes, come in.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:50.390
What is it?

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:59.440
We thought you might like this...

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:03.910
You look so down, so...

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.730
Commander, if there's anything we can do, please tell us.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.670
That's just a scarab beetle{dung beetle} that you can find anywhere. {Re-time!}

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.750
If you have time to worry about me, use it to rest your bodies.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.050
We still have battles to fight.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.650
If you understand, leave.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:30.480
Emile, sorry I dragged you along.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:32.640
It's all right.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:36.640
I thought it was a good idea, too...

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:37.340
Yeah...

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.730
The Commander's just trying to act tough.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:46.510
Really?

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.240
Yes.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.790
Why did he say something like that then?

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:54.040
Something like "If you have time to worry about me..."

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.540
That's because...

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:01.420
If the commander doesn't act strong, he probably won't be able to keep going.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.300
We have to try our best and support him then.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.120
What?

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:13.740
You sure say some cute things, don't ya?

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.320
H-Hey!

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:23.150
Isara!

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:25.190
Isara!

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:27.080
She's having a nightmare again...

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:29.310
Isara is... Someone, come and-

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:30.500
Corporal Stark,

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.320
everything's all right now.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.580
This is the Hamatoriya Base. {Yep, sounds like Hamatoriya. Did much research but to no avail. I'll leave it as it is.}

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:54.660
Isara!

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:07.070
Welkin... said he would come sometime soon.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.490
Sorry I couldn't attend her funeral.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.940
It's okay. You had no choice.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.920
Everyone's probably blaming me, aren't they?

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:21.010
No way! Why?

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:23.740
Everybody's worried about you.

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:27.420
They want you to get well soon and sing for everybody.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:29.460
Sing...

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:33.220
How are you feeling?

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:34.700
I don't know.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:38.470
Should I leave?

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:39.770
No.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:42.270
It's better if both of you hear this.

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:55.030
Isara, hold on tight! The medic will be here soon!

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.290
You'll be all right! It barely grazed you!

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.460
I can't believe you.

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:08.210
You gave me a doll,

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:10.720
yet you didn't bother to keep one for yourself?

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:14.840
Here. Hold it tightly.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:24.680
I... love your songs, Rosie...

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:27.900
Although it was only once... I'm glad I could hear it...

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.910
What're you talking about?

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:32.360
At a time like this...

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:34.670
What do you want to hear?

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:37.330
As long as you're willing to listen, I'll sing anything!

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:38.870
As many times as you'd like!

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:43.830
I'm happy... {:'-(}

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:51.850
Isara...

00:07:58.670 --> 00:07:59.580
Isara...

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:06.420
Why?

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.150
Why was she able to smile?

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:11.610
On the verge of death...

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:20.660
I shouldn't keep this.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:23.020
I'll return it to you instead.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:27.300
That belongs to you, Rosie.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:28.460
If I had...

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:32.510
If I had been more alert, Isara would still be alive!

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:34.380
She wouldn't have died! {Added this line in. -Ky}

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.990
I should've been shot instead!

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:38.670
Rosie...

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:40.510
Don't blame yourself.

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:45.440
Isara lived her own life as best she could.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:47.440
It's no one's fault.

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:50.180
I feel like Isara was happy.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:03.160
This, huh?

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:09.140
The victory at Mulberry Beach was due to Squad 7's smoke bombs.

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.940
A victory, you say?

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:12.980
Well, eh...

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:14.570
Well, whatever.

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:17.600
Take me to the person who made them!

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:21.130
I wonder why the general gathered us?

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:24.410
Is he going to give us medals?

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:27.270
Isara would definitely be happy too.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:31.340
Who made the smoke bombs?

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:35.550
What's wrong? Hurry and answer me!

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:41.010
The creator was killed in action during the battle for Mulberry Beach.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:43.010
Killed in action?

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:45.060
Is there anyone else who knows how to make them then?

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:46.300
No Sir!

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:49.230
She created those on her own.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.260
There should be memos or something at least! Find them!

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:05.000
Why is there a symbol for those dirty Darcsens here?!

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:10.460
That's because Isara Gunther was a Darcsen.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:15.150
Don't display something like this while I'm around!

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:19.550
Get off!

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:25.700
Can't you feel the slightest bit of grief over the death of a soldier from the militia?!

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:27.140
You maggot!

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:29.310
Y-You!

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:35.400
You dare defy a general such as myself?!

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:40.930
Fool! I'll teach you a lesson!

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:41.990
Please wait!

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.660
I apologize for her rudeness.

00:10:47.650 --> 00:10:51.100
Please punish me instead.

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:53.610
All right then.

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:59.780
2nd Lieutenant Welkin Gunther, procure the blueprints for the new smoke bombs within the next few days.

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:02.610
If you can't, then I'll treat it as a military offence!

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:10.060
I can't believe he talked that way about Isara...

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:11.110
Welkin.

00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:13.490
You didn't have to apologize.

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:17.320
If I didn't apologize, Rosie would have been punished.

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:20.080
But...

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:22.740
I'll bear all the responsibility.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:39.260
Rosie fell asleep.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:43.420
She said she would return to the barracks after she had her bandages changed.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:56.980
Brother, be careful.

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:06.310
Make it a bit wider.

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:07.820
Yeah, got it.

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:10.960
How much deeper should it be?

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:12.880
The deeper the better.

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:15.580
Wait, what are you guys doing?

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:17.470
Alicia.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:20.520
We want to teach that maggot a lesson.

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:26.030
I know he's always the first to exit from here every Thursday morning.

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:28.420
What'll we do if he finds out?

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:29.930
He's a general!

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:32.060
Are you saying we can't do this just because he's a general?

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:37.080
This is a matter concerning Squad 7's pride!

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:40.650
If you guys want to protest, there are other ways, aren't there?

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:42.320
We've already decided on this!

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:46.070
If you want to stop us, then go ahead and tell General Damon!

00:12:50.780 --> 00:12:52.750
Let them do what they want.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.080
We can't!

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:58.130
You should have a proper talk with them and stop them.

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:00.990
You tried to stop them, but it was useless, right?

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.340
Just let them do it then.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:06.060
Is it all right if they get punished then?

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:08.060
I'll take responsibility for them.

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:11.430
That's not what a commander should be responsible for!

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:13.330
What then?

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:16.200
You're taking responsibility for everything all on your own.

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:19.520
That'll only distance yourself from everyone, won't it?

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:22.340
Wasn't it you who always wanted me...

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:24.490
...to act more like a commander?

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:28.300
It's getting late.

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:30.440
You should go back to the barracks and sleep.

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:34.220
Why?

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:37.000
We're comrades, right?

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:40.420
Why won't you share your sorrow with us?

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:46.740
I know you're more upset than anyone else over Isara's death!

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:51.660
I don't expect you to understand my feelings.

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:55.910
I'm grateful that you're worried about me,

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:57.730
but could you leave me alone?

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:58.730
No!

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:01.150
Why?

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:03.150
It doesn't matter. Do you need a reason?

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:05.160
I don't get what you're-

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:07.050
It's because I like you!

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:31.830
<i>Ragnite?</i>

00:14:35.990 --> 00:14:37.100
<i>Why is it shining?</i>

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:47.590
Alicia, what on earth happened?

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:52.660
Did something happen between you and Welkin?

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:57.220
I'll get him.

00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:58.120
Wait.

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:01.060
I don't care about him.

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:03.340
But everyone else is...

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:09.090
What's the matter?

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:14.760
Squad 7 is quite hardworking, huh?

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.930
You won't be able to stop us.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:18.770
No, I don't plan to stop you guys.

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:23.020
I just feel like this is too inefficient.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:25.230
Inefficient?

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:31.250
I know you guys hate that fat, arrogant, bag of wind.

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:36.200
This is a good trap if you want to wipe the smirk off that snob's face. {Combined these lines. -Ky}

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:37.330
Then...

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:39.580
But it's not the best idea.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:44.100
Why? It's because guys like him are everywhere in the army.

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:46.060
Even if you humiliate Damon and drive him out,

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:48.950
another Damon will come in his place.

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:50.530
Isn't that right?

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:55.050
What should we do then?

00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:57.690
We'll win!

00:15:57.690 --> 00:16:00.980
We'll keep winning battles, and return peace to Gallia!

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:04.410
Only then will Isara's death not be in vain!

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:37.960
That's...

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:40.130
You know what it is?

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:43.130
I saw her make it.

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:43.950
I see.

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:47.380
She was singing happily back then.

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:49.550
A Darcsen song, right?

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:51.430
You know about it?

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:53.530
Isara really liked it.

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:57.180
Although it's a bit late,

00:16:57.180 --> 00:16:58.920
I'll fulfill it right now. {is it "I"? or could it be "your wish will be realized right now"}

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:01.080
That wish of yours.

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:14.610
<i>Endlessly, the light</i>

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:22.280
<i>continues shining brightly.</i>

00:17:23.550 --> 00:17:30.860
<i>Illuminating tomorrow.</i>

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:37.700
<i>Deep inside my heart,</i>

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:45.680
<i>I think of my birth place.</i>

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:54.450
<i>Even if tears flow</i>

00:17:54.450 --> 00:18:01.080
<i>the sky remains blue.</i>

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:05.260
<i>No matter what kind of world it is,</i>

00:18:05.260 --> 00:18:12.220
<i>we can believe in love.</i>

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:19.860
<i>And live on...</i>

00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:50.310
What's up with you?

00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:53.970
You're just like a drenched Gallia mountain cat.

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:58.600
What's wrong? I tried your way of talking.

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:00.240
What do you want? It's late.

00:19:00.810 --> 00:19:02.190
Did Alicia send you?

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:05.800
Well, something like that.

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:09.000
How about interacting with the kids more?

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.340
You're the commander, after all.

00:19:11.070 --> 00:19:13.670
I don't have the right to be called a commander.

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:16.630
I couldn't even protect Isara.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:18.990
Hey, Welkin, don't joke around.

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:23.090
Three people have already been discharged from Squad 1.

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:25.630
There are people who're bed-ridden too.

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:30.440
But I've never once said that I couldn't protect them!

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:32.560
Are you a god?

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:33.680
A hero?

00:19:34.390 --> 00:19:35.870
Who do you think you are?

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:39.550
If you still don't understand, then let me tell you.

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:42.850
You're just a dumbass who's wallowing in self-pity!

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:46.330
You're right. I'm not a hero or anything.

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:49.870
Is that why you ignored your squad members and made Alicia cry?!

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:52.020
You're here, aren't you?

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:53.180
Faldio.

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:13.050
Yo! My name is Zaka.

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:16.850
I always keep my right eye closed, but it's not because my right eye can't see.

00:20:16.850 --> 00:20:21.890
I was in charge of measuring and surveying in a factory before, so I got used to looking at things with one eye.

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:26.020
Darcsens are skillful with their hands.

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:28.710
I'm quite good at metalworking. {not machines, but art made from... do a search on google it's quite interesting}

00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:31.540
Next on Valkyria Chronicles,

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:34.320
Chapter 19: Tears.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:40.000
Chapter 19

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:40.000
Tears

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:38.950
Hatred and vengeance will not make anyone happy.
